    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1/1 test passing).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `displayName` field flows through the same `OwnerDto`/`OwnerMapper` used by both the create (`POST`) and read (`GET`) responses, so the fix is in two places:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` response schema, so the OpenAPI generator emits `getDisplayName()`/`setDisplayName()` on `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct mapping that computes it from the stored entity names:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\",\n           expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nThis formats `displayName` exactly as `LastName, FirstName` from the persisted `Owner`. The acceptance test (`AcceptanceTest.coreComputesDisplayName`) creates an owner and reads back `$.displayName` == `\"<lastName>, John\"`, which now passes.\n\nNo new OfficeFloor functions were needed \u2014 the existing `RespondWithOwnerCreated`/`RespondWithOwner` steps already delegate to `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, so the derived field appears in every owner response.",
